<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>New longitude after sailing along a parallel</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A ship at [[if test="is(ix=1)"]]\((20^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 42^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]\((35^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 8^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]\((48^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 60^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]\((25^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 3^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]\((40^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 70^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]\((15^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 30^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]\((65^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 5^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]\((28^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 95^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]\((55^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 20^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]\((10^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 50^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]] sails due [[if test="is(dir=1)"]]east[[else]]west[[/if]] along its parallel at \({@v@}\) knots for \({@t@}\) hours.</p><p>(a) Find the distance sailed.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] nm [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the change in longitude, in degrees correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Find the new longitude, in degrees correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans3]] \(^\circ\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Distance \(=\) speed \(\times\) time \(= {@v@} \times {@t@} = {@dist@}\) nm.</p><p>(b) On the parallel \({@phi@}^\circ\), one degree of longitude is \(60\cos {@phi@}^\circ\) nm long, so the change in longitude is</p><p>\[\frac{ {@dist@} }{60 \cos {@phi@}^\circ} = {@dispdp(float(dl),3)@} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(10*dl+1/2)/10),1)@}^\circ.\]</p><p>(c) The ship sails [[if test="is(dir=1)"]]east[[else]]west[[/if]], so [[if test="is(dir=1)"]]an east longitude increases and a west one decreases.[[else]]a west longitude increases and an east one decreases.[[/if]][[if test="xgr"]] It crosses the Greenwich meridian, so the letter changes.[[/if]] New longitude: \({@dispdp(float(floor(10*lon1+1/2)/10),1)@}^\circ\,\mathrm{[[if test="e1"]]E[[else]]W[[/if]]}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[cosd(x) := cos(x*%pi/180);
sind(x) := sin(x*%pi/180);
atand(x) := 180*atan(x)/%pi;
asind(x) := 180*asin(x)/%pi;
two(v) := if v < 10 then sconcat("0", string(v)) else string(v);
hm(m) := block([q], q: mod(m, 1440), sconcat(two(floor(q/60)), ":", two(mod(q, 60))));
dmx(m) := sconcat(string(floor(m/60)), "^\\circ", two(mod(m, 60)), "'");
/* Design: change of longitude after sailing along a parallel, from speed and time. [phi, N/S, l0, E/W, direction (1 east, -1 west), speed, hours]. Signed longitudes, east positive. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), chapter 3, Exercise E question 5. */
L: [[20,"S",42,"E",1,15,36],[35,"N",8,"W",1,18,30],[48,"S",60,"E",-1,12,48],[25,"N",3,"E",-1,14,24],[40,"S",70,"E",1,16,40],[15,"N",30,"W",-1,20,30],[65,"N",5,"W",1,10,36],[28,"S",95,"E",-1,22,25],[55,"N",20,"W",-1,11,40],[10,"S",50,"E",1,13,45]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
E: L[ix];
phi: E[1]; l0: E[3]; dir: E[5]; v: E[6]; t: E[7];
g0: if E[4]="E" then l0 else -l0;
e0: is(E[4]="E");
dist: v*t;
dl: dist/(60*cosd(phi));
g1: g0+dir*dl;
lon1: abs(g1);
ew1: if g1>0 then "E" else "W";
e1: is(g1>0);
xgr: is(g0*g1<0);
eww: if e1 then "W" else "E";
/* diagnostics */
nc: dist/60; mc: dist*cosd(phi)/60; sn: dist/(60*sind(phi));
wd: g0-dir*dl;
ew2: if wd>0 then "E" else "W";
ga: g0+dir*(float(floor(10*dl+1/2)/10)+1.5);
ewa: if ga>0 then "E" else "W";
opt4: [["E", e1, "E"], ["W", not e1, "W"]];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
